                                                                            Layer 5
                                                                        fusion engine

The Problem: 
The most significant flaw in traditional environmental monitoring is the "Single Point of Failure." If a single smoke sensor breaks, or a single camera glitches, it triggers a false alarm. Dispatching a drone or a fire truck based on a single sensor wastes thousands of dollars.

The Solution: 
The Sensor Fusion Engine. It acts as a central cognitive brain that refuses to panic. It utilizes a Deterministic Logic Matrix (a weighted scoring system) to build a chain of evidence.

The Action:

It listens to all incoming telemetry via the MQTT broker.

It assigns a specific point value to different types of evidence (Space, Heat, Motion, Biology).

It dynamically updates the system's State Machine (DORMANT → PRE-ALERT → WATCH → INVESTIGATE → CRITICAL).

Only when the Threat Score breaches 100 points does it authorize the automated UAV dispatch.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Implementation:
Hardware:a centralized Raspberry Pi acting as the local server.
Software: A Python backend script using the paho-mqtt library.

The Weighted Scoring Matrix:

NASA Satellite Anomaly (WAKE_UP) = +20 Points

ESP32 Local Temp Spike (ANOMALY_CONFIRMED) = +30 Points

mmWave Radar Movement (MOTION_CONFIRMED) = +30 Points

YOLOv8 Biological/Visual Anomaly (CRITICAL_HAZARD_VERIFIED) = +40 Points

(Total possible score = 120. Threshold to deploy UAV = 100).
